<h1>Serbian Inflectional  Grammar</h1>Version of September 11, 2026, 2:06 pm<br />Documentation available at <a href="http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar" target="_blank">http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar</a><br />Tagset available at <a href="../dictionary/export_tagset.php" target="_blank">Export UNDL Foundation tagset</a>.<br /><br /><b>M0</b><br />Invariant<br /><br /><b>M1</b><br />Irregular: rules are defined inside the entry in the dictionary<br /><br /><b>M2</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns with consonant endings (excluding those that end in velar consonants -k,-g,-h, those that have a fleeting -a-, those that end in a palatal consonants,and those whose base form is expanded by -ov- or -ev- in plural). (<i>medved, mrav, predmet</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"e";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PAU:=0>"a";<br /><br /><b>M3</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns with consonant endings (excluding those that end in velar consonants -k,-g,-h, those that have a fleeting -a-, and those that end in a palatal consonants) whose base form is expanded by -ov- in plural. (<i>dlan, cvet, stan</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"e";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"ova";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"ove";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ovima";<br /> PAU:=0>"a";<br /><br /><b>M4</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns with palatal consonants endings (except those that have a fleeting -a-) whose base form is expanded by -ev- in plural. (<i>muž, kralj, ključ</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"em";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"evi";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"eva";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"evima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"eve";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"evi";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"evima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"evima";<br /> PAU:=0>"a";<br /><br /><b>M5</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns with palatal consonants endings (those that have a fleeting -a-) whose base form is not expanded by -ev- in plural. (<i>prijatelj, vozač</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"em";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PAU:=0>"a";<br /><br /><b>M6</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns ending with -k (except those having a fleeting -a-), whose base is not expanded with -ov- or -ev- in plural forms.  (<i>učenik, vojnik</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:="k">"če";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:="k">"ci";<br /> PLR&GNT:="">"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:="k">"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:="">"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="k">"ci";<br /> PLR&INS:="k">"cima";<br /> PLR&LOC:="k">"cima";<br /> PAU:=0>"a";<br /><br /><b>M7</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns ending with -g (except those having a fleeting -a-), whose base is not expanded with -ov- or -ev- in plural forms. (<i>kovčeg</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:="g">"že";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:="g">"zi";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:="g">"zima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="g">"zi";<br /> PLR&INS:="g">"zima";<br /> PLR&LOC:="g">"zima";<br /> PAU:=0>"a";<br /><br /><b>M8</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns ending with -h (except those having a fleeting -a-), whose base is not expanded with -ov- or -ev- in plural forms. (<i>siromah, orah</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"še";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br />PLR&NOM:=1>"si";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"sima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"si";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"sima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"sima";<br /> PAU:=0>"a";<br /><br /><b>M9</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns ending with sonant/voiceless consonant + fleeting -a- + c (<i>udarac, lovac, borac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="ac">"ca";<br /> SNG&DAT:="ac">"cu";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:="ac">"ca";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:= "ac">"če";<br /> SNG&INS:="ac">"cem";<br /> SNG&LOC:="ac">"cu";<br />PLR&NOM:="ac">"ci";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:="ac">"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:="ac">"ce";<br /> PLR&VOC:= "ac">"ci";<br /> PLR&INS:="ac">"cima";<br /> PLR&LOC:="ac">"cima";<br /> PAU:="ac">"ca";<br /><br /><b>M10</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns ending with -lac, such that the alternation of -l- into -o- occurs. (<i>gledalac, čitalac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="lac">"oca";<br /> SNG&DAT:="lac">"ocu";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:="lac">"oca";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:="lac">"oče";<br /> SNG&INS:="lac">"ocem";<br /> SNG&LOC:="lac">"ocu";<br /> PLR&NOM:="lac">"oci";<br /> PLR&GNT:=>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:="lac">"ocima";<br /> PLR&ACC:="lac">"oce";<br /> PLR&VOC:= "lac">"oci";<br /> PLR&INS:="lac">"ocima";<br /> PLR&LOC:="lac">"ocima";<br /> PAU:="lac">"oca";<br /><br /><b>M11</b><br />According to this paradigm are inflected masculine nouns ending with -tak, containing fleeting -a-, and with cluster reduction of -t-. (<i>ostatak, dodatak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="ak">"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:="ak">"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC&ANM:="ak">"ka";<br /> SNG&ACC&NANM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:="tak">"če";<br /> SNG&INS:="ak">"kom";<br /> SNG&LOC:="tak">"tku";<br /> PLR&NOM:="tak">"ci";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:="tak">"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:="ak">"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:= "tak">"ci";<br /> PLR&INS:="tak">"cima";<br /> PLR&LOC:="tak">"cima";<br /> PAU:="ak">"ka";<br /><br /><b>M12</b><br />Neuter gender nouns that do not have a base form expansion with -n- or -t- in dependent cases and that do not have a fleeting -a-. (<i>more, polje</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=1>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"m";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&GNT:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ima";<br /> PAU:=1>"a";<br /><br /><b>M13</b><br />Neuter gender nouns with -o ending that contain the fleeting -a- and that do not have base form expansion with -t- or -n- in dependent cases. (<i>jutro, jedro</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=1>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"m";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"u";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&GNT:="a"<[-2],1>"a";<br />  PLR&DAT:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ima";<br /> PAU:=1>"a";<br /><br /><b>M14</b><br />Neuter gender nouns that have a base form expansion with -n- in dependent cases. (<i>rame, vreme, ime</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"na";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"nu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"nom";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"nu";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"nima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"nima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"nima";<br /> PAU:=0>"na";<br /><br /><b>M15</b><br />Neuter gender nouns that have a base form expansion with -t- in dependent cases. (<i>bure, kube, uže</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=1>"eta";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"etu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"etom";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"etu";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"eta";<br /> PLR&GNT:=1>"eta";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"etima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"eta";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"eta";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"etima";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"etima";<br /> PAU:=1>"eta";<br /><br /><b>M16</b><br />Feminine gender nouns that do not have -k-,-g- or -h- immediately before the -a ending; that do not end with -ica and that do not have a fleeting -a-. (<i>žena</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="a">"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="a">"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:="a">"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:="a">"o";<br /> SNG&INS:="a">"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:="a">"i";<br /> PLR&NOM:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&ACC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ma";<br /> PAU:="a">"e";<br /><br /><b>M17</b><br />Feminine gender nouns with a fleeting -a- and that do not have a -k-, -g- or -h- immediately before the ending -a. (<i>ovca</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="a">"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="a">"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:="a">"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:="a">"o";<br /> SNG&INS:="a">"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:="a">"i";<br /> PLR&NOM:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&GNT:="a"<[-2];<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&ACC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ma";<br /> PAU:="a">"e";<br /><br /><b>M18</b><br />Feminine gender nouns containing more than two syllables and ending with -ica. (<i>učiteljica</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="a">"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="a">"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:="a">"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:="a">"e";<br /> SNG&INS:="a">"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:="a">"i";<br /> PLR&NOM:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&ACC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ma";<br /> PAU:="a">"e";<br /><br /><b>M19</b><br />Feminine gender nouns ending with -ka without a fleeting -a- or a consonant cluster. (<i>pavlaka, navlaka</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="a">"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="ka">"ci";<br /> SNG&ACC:="a">"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:="a">"o";<br /> SNG&INS:="a">"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:="ka">"ci";<br /> PLR&NOM:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&ACC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ma";<br /> PAU:="a">"e";<br /><br /><b>M20</b><br />Feminine gender nouns ending with -ga without a fleeting -a- or a consonant cluster. (<i>snaga, knjiga</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="a">"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="ga">"zi";<br /> SNG&ACC:="a">"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:="a">"o";<br /> SNG&INS:="a">"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:="ga">"zi";<br /> PLR&NOM:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&GNT:=>"";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&ACC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ma";<br /> PAU:="a">"e";<br /><br /><b>M21</b><br />Feminine gender nouns ending with -ha without a fleeting -a- or a consonant cluster. (<i>snaha</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:="a">"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="ha">"si";<br /> SNG&ACC:="a">"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:="a">"o";<br /> SNG&INS:="a">"om";<br /> SNG&LOC:="ha">"si";<br /> PLR&NOM:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&ACC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:="a">"e";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ma";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ma";<br /> PAU:="a">"e";<br /><br /><b>M22</b><br />Feminine gender nouns ending in a consonant. (<i>stvar</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&LOC: